,"lo":19.2348,"a":"XVII, Uszoda utca 2","h":"Mon–Fri 06:00–22:00, Sat Sun 07:00–17:00","pr":"Adult: ; senior, student:","b":""},{"n":"Hungarian National Gallery","k":"see","la":47.49623,"lo":19.03977,"a":"I, Szent György tér 2","h":"Tue-Sun 10:00–18:00","pr":"Permanent exhibitions for adult: ; for senior, student: . Temporary exhibition f","b":"Houses an astounding collection of paintings. For those interested in Hungarian artists, this is the museum to visit. It was established in 1957 as the national art museum. Its collections cover Hungarian art in all genres, including…"},{"n":"Palatinal Crypt","k":"see","la":47.49631,"lo":19.03953,"a":"Within the Hungarian National Gallery","h":"Only by appointment","pr":"","b":"Burial place of the Hungarian branch of the Habsburg dynasty, founded by Archduke Joseph, Palatine of Hungary. It is the only interior part of Royal Palace which survived the destruction of World War II and was not demolished during the…"},{"n":"Castle Museum","k":"see","la":47.49515,"lo":19.04021,"a":"I, Szent György tér 2","h":"Tue–Sun 10:00–18:00","pr":"Adult: ; senior, student:","b":"It's the Medieval Department of the Budapest History Museum. Permanent exhibitions, over four floors: ancient people, antique cultures and temporary exhibitions. The restored part of the medieval castle, including the Royal Chapel and…"},{"n":"Castle Chapel","k":"see","la":47.49543,"lo":19.04067,"a":"Within the Castle Museum","h":"Tue–Sun 10:00–18:00","pr":"","b":"The chapel was built by Sigismund of Luxembourg in the 15th century as the lower chapel of the former castle church. The Gothic chapel, which survived the destruction of the siege of 1686, was buried under a Baroque terrace for…"},{"n":"Saint Stephen's Hall","k":"see","la":47.49506,"lo":19.04005,"a":"I, Szent György tér 2","h":"Tue–Sun 10:00–18:00","pr":"Adult: ; senior, student:","b":"A richly decorated hall was built in 1902. It was destroyed in World War II, and rebuilt in 2021."},{"n":"National Széchényi Library","k":"see","la":47.4953,"lo":19.0395,"a":"I, Szent György tér 4-5-6","h":"Tue–Sat 09:00–20:00","pr":"","b":"The library was founded in 1802 by the highly patriotic Hungarian aristocrat Count Ferenc Széchényi. Széchényi traveled the world buying Hungarian books, which he assembled and donated to the nation. In the following year the public…"},{"n":"Habsburg Gate","k":"see","la":47.49733,"lo":19.03865,"a":"I, Szent György tér","h":"","pr":"","b":"The ornate Neo-Baroque gate separating the Royal Palace and the Castle Quarter. It was built between 1903 and 1905 according to plans of Alajos Hauszmann. The iron lattice of the gate was made by Gyula Jungfer. It was seriously damaged…"},{"n":"Fountain of Fishing Kids","k":"see","la":47.49713,"lo":19.0388,"a":"I, Savoy Terrace","h":"","pr":"","b":"This is the work of sculptor Károly Senyei from 1912. It depicts two children grappling with a fish. The fine workmanship of the fishing net is remarkable."},{"n":"Equestrian Statue of Prince Eugene of Savoy","k":"see","la":47.49639,"lo":19.04008,"a":"I, Savoy Terrace","h":"","pr":"","b":"The Neo-Baroque statue was made by sculptor József Róna for the town of Zenta, but the town could not afford the price. The monument was bought in 1900 as a temporary solution until the planned equestrian statue of King Franz Joseph was…"},{"n":"Fountain of King Matthias","k":"see","la":47.49611,"lo":19.03909,"a":"I, Hunyadi Court","h":"","pr":"","b":"This spectacular fountain shows a group of hunters led by King Matthias Corvinus together with hounds, a killed deer, Galeotto Marzio with a hawk, and Ilonka Szép with a doe. This group of people stands between fallen rocks with water…"},{"n":"Lion's Gate","k":"see","la":47.49578,"lo":19.03934,"a":"I, Lion's Court","h":"","pr":"","b":"Two pairs of lions guard the monumental gate leading into Lion's Court. The four statues are the works of János Fadrusz from 1901. The animals standing on the outer side of the gate are menacing, while the inner ones are calm and…"},{"n":"Royal Guard","k":"see","la":47.49607,"lo":19.0386,"a":"I, Hunyadi Court","h":"Fri–Sun 11:00–18:00","pr":"Adult: ; senior, student:","b":"It was built in 1903 according to plans of Alajos Hauszmann. It was hit by a bomb in World War II, and was demolished in 1971. It was rebuilt between 2017–2021. There is an exhibition about history of the Royal Guard."},{"n":"Royal Riding Hall","k":"see","la":47.49592,"lo":19.03806,"a":"I, Lovarda utca","h":"","pr":"","b":"The Neo-Baroque riding hall was built between 1901 and 1903 in parallel with the construction of the Royal Palace. It was hit by a bomb in World War II, and was demolished in 1954. Rebuilt between 2017–2020. It's used as an event venue."},{"n":"Horse Brainer Statue","k":"see","la":47.49574,"lo":19.03838,"a":"I, Horse Brainer Court","h":"","pr":"","b":"The statue of the Hortobágy horseherd taming a wild horse used to stand in front of the Royal Riding Hall. It is the work of György Vastagh from 1901. The statue was displayed in the Exposition Universelle in Paris (1900). The damaged…"},{"n":"The Hauszmann Story exhibition","k":"see","la":47.49675,"lo":19.03844,"a":"I, Szent György tér 2","h":"Tue–Sun 10:00–18:00","pr":"Free entrance","b":"The exhibition commemorates the life and the greatest work of the architect Alajos Hauszmann."}],"eat":[{"n":"Trófea Grill","k":"eat","la":null,"lo":null,"a":"","h":"","pr":"","b":"The best among all-you-can-eat (buffet) and all the alcohol you can drink. Best to book a table in advance. Has 4 locations. 1 on Buda downtown by Margaret Bridge (Margit körút 2)"},{"n":"Leroy Cafe","k":"eat","la":null,"lo":null,"a":"Pest (5 locations), Buda (3 locations)","h":"","pr":"","b":"(See district article Pest for details) Mid- to high-priced restaurant chain that offers Hungarian classics with other Italian and European cuisine. Very fashionable interiors and popular with the well-paid white collar crowd.…"},{"n":"Erzsébetliget Restaurant","k":"eat","la":47.50836,